  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 100 AM CDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nAs our cool surface high pressure system shifts further to the\neast, we'll see one more day of cool temps/low humidity pleasantry\nbefore stifling summer heat re-emerges. In between will be a \nchance of rain/storms heading into the weekend. NAEFS-ESAT \nindicates PW's increasing to 2\" with 2-5 year Return Intervals, \nsuggesting locally heavy/efficient downpours will be the main \nstorm threat for peak pop times late Friday night into Saturday.\n\nThe strong Western U.S. upper ridge pattern becomes more of an \ninfluence upon our sensible weather next week, returning highs \nAOA 90F for the entirety of the week. Max high pressure \ninfluence here is early in the week, with highs in the mid-upper\n90s and HI's 100-110F. A subtle retrograde of the high as the \nweek wears on softens the heat's blow to lower half 90s over its\nback half close-out.",
